  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_23' aria-label=\" K.S. Muralidhar versus R. Subbulakshmi & Anr. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('23','2024','2024_11_835_849','2024INSC886'); ><font size='4'> <strong>K.S. MURALIDHAR<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>R. SUBBULAKSHMI & ANR. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 11 S.C.R. 835</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 886</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010006782024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : C.T. RAVIKUMAR<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SANJAY KAROL</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Matter pertains to the enhancement of compensation towards pain and suffering for a motor accident victim having suffered 100% disability. Headnotes&dagger; Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 &ndash; Motor accident &ndash; Compensation &ndash; Enhancement of &ndash; Victim aged company vehicle which collided with container lorry driven rashly and negligently &ndash; Victim suffered 90% permanent disability &ndash; Tribunal taking the functional disability as 100%, awarded compensation of Rs.58,09,930/- with 6% interest per annum and Rs.1,00,000/- as future medical<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 22-11-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 12993/2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('23','2024','2024_11_835_849','2024INSC886','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href